{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03331",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.74,
      "end_seconds": 7.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.48,
      "end_seconds": 12.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.7,
      "end_seconds": 23.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so hello, doctor. I hope it's alright if I stay in for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.55,
      "end_seconds": 28.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.03,
      "end_seconds": 34.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a high temperature."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.46,
      "end_seconds": 38.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.15,
      "end_seconds": 52.02,
      "duration_seconds": 11.87,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.67,
      "end_seconds": 56.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.93,
      "end_seconds": 63.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.06,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly. And a sore mouth as well, since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.54,
      "end_seconds": 67.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Have you been feeling very weak?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.98,
      "end_seconds": 69.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Mm, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.81,
      "end_seconds": 73.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "How much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.89,
      "end_seconds": 82.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.92,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.76,
      "end_seconds": 88.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.91,
      "end_seconds": 92.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.09,
      "end_seconds": 96.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Have you noticed rash or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.64,
      "end_seconds": 111.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.94,
      "text": "No, no rash, no diarrhoea. I did have shaking chills at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.35,
      "end_seconds": 118.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "What about cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.36,
      "end_seconds": 121.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "No. No cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 121.94,
      "end_seconds": 126.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice cough. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.58,
      "end_seconds": 135.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "Okay, so no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.16,
      "end_seconds": 142.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.84,
      "end_seconds": 146.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.73,
      "end_seconds": 150.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.4,
      "end_seconds": 154.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.41,
      "end_seconds": 156.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.57,
      "end_seconds": 160.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.85,
      "end_seconds": 169.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.66,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.96,
      "end_seconds": 184.16,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.14,
      "end_seconds": 187.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.89,
      "end_seconds": 192.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.57,
      "end_seconds": 194.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.69,
      "end_seconds": 202.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.31,
      "end_seconds": 204.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.63,
      "end_seconds": 209.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.77,
      "end_seconds": 215.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Right, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.03,
      "end_seconds": 229.91,
      "duration_seconds": 10.88,
      "text": "I've, I've got thin bones. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I have an enlarged prostate, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.27,
      "end_seconds": 232.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.94,
      "end_seconds": 240.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Alright, thin bones and an enlarged prostate, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.1,
      "end_seconds": 262.45,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.29,
      "end_seconds": 273.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "It's, It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.51,
      "end_seconds": 277.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.5,
      "end_seconds": 294.86,
      "duration_seconds": 16.36,
      "text": "For my bones, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Mm, I'm on tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate. It's chemotherapy last week, recent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 296.12,
      "end_seconds": 305.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Respiratory rate 18, temperature 36.7, oxygen saturation is 97 percent. BP is 96 over 56, heart rate 93."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.03,
      "end_seconds": 309.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.94,
      "end_seconds": 315.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.02,
      "end_seconds": 320.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.64,
      "end_seconds": 343.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "You are hot, shaking and your blood pressure is low, and you had chemotherapy nine days ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.09,
      "end_seconds": 348.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.27,
      "end_seconds": 368.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: I'd lean towards neutropenic sepsis. A chest infection is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.98,
      "end_seconds": 373.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.2,
      "end_seconds": 391.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.28,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now neutropenic sepsis is my leading thought, not anything worse. I want urgent blood tests done, that's for neutropenic sepsis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.05,
      "end_seconds": 394.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.91,
      "end_seconds": 411.77,
      "duration_seconds": 15.86,
      "text": "Let's use piperacillin and tazobactam, 4.5 grams, now, single dose. That's for neutropenic sepsis. This is an emergency, antibiotics are being given within the hour. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.4,
      "end_seconds": 416.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.87,
      "end_seconds": 424.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}